{
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Turn removable storage into physical game cartridges",
    "homepage": "https://github.com/HarryBMa/pc-gamepak",
    "license": "MIT",
    "architecture": {
        "64bit": {
            "url": "https://github.com/HarryBMa/pc-gamepak/releases/download/v1.0.0/pc-gamepak-1.0.0-windows-x86_64.zip",
            "hash": "82fcf997982d3053d7ba0cac703624bb104c45ec42a6b5f70dfba5df8627d153",
            "extract_dir": "pc-gamepak-1.0.0-windows-x86_64"
        }
    },
    "bin": [
        "pc-gamepak.exe",
        "pc-gamepak-watcher.exe"
    ],
    "notes": [
        "The wizard works straight away, with no further setup:",
        "",
        "    pc-gamepak --create",
        "",
        "The watcher is what opens a launcher when a cartridge is plugged in.",
        "Scoop cannot register it to start at logon, so run the installer once:",
        "",
        "    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \"$dir\\windows\\install.ps1\" -Mode Watcher",
        "",
        "-Mode Watcher matters: without it the script asks which mode to install",
        "and a non-interactive shell cannot answer.",
        "",
        "To undo that later:  powershell -File \"$dir\\windows\\uninstall.ps1\""
    ],
    "checkver": {
        "github": "https://github.com/HarryBMa/pc-gamepak"
    },
    "autoupdate": {
        "architecture": {
            "64bit": {
                "url": "https://github.com/HarryBMa/pc-gamepak/releases/download/v$version/pc-gamepak-$version-windows-x86_64.zip",
                "extract_dir": "pc-gamepak-$version-windows-x86_64"
            }
        },
        "hash": {
            "url": "$url.sha256"
        }
    }
}
